course: dictionary
lesson: 1809
title: Clover and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words in a text are new to you, but the words around them often give you the meaning. Clover is one of these words. «Clover leaves usually have three leaflets, and four-leaf clovers are rare, about one in many thousands.» The word leaves tells you clover is a plant with leaves, and the word leaflets, next to three, tells you each leaf is made of smaller parts.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence before you look in the dictionary. «Wild rabbits mostly eat grass, clover and leafy plants.» Clover is listed with grass and leafy plants, so it must be a plant that rabbits can eat. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning in place of the new word and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words have a special meaning in certain phrases. «Be in clover» means to live in comfort, with plenty of everything you need. The phrase does not mean that you are standing in a field of clover, so the clue is in the whole phrase, not just one word. When context is not enough, check the dictionary.
fact: Clover is a small wild plant with leaves made of three round parts.
fact: A four-leaf clover is a rare clover leaf with four parts, and it is said to bring good luck.
fact: Clover flowers are small white, pink or purple heads, and bees love them.
fact: Farmers grow clover for animals to eat, and it helps to make the soil richer.
fact: The shamrock, a little clover with three leaves, is linked with Ireland.
exercise: «Clover leaves usually have three leaflets, and four-leaf clovers are rare.» What does the sentence tell you about four-leaf clovers? | They have five leaflets each | *They are rare | They are the usual kind of clover | They grow in every garden
exercise: «Longer, unmown grass lets clover, daisies and other flowers bloom and feed bees and butterflies.» What does bloom mean here? | To be cut short | *To produce flowers | To turn brown in the sun | To sink into the soil
exercise: «Farmers plant clover or beans to make the soil richer.» Why do farmers plant clover? | To keep the soil wet and cold | To cover the soil with stones | *To make the soil better for plants to grow | To make a lucky charm
test: «Clover, peas and beans have little lumps on their roots full of helpful bacteria that take nitrogen from the air and turn it into plant food.» What do the lumps on the roots do? | Make the flowers bloom | Give the plant sugar | Keep rabbits away | *Turn nitrogen from the air into plant food
test: Lucy says a four-leaf clover is a lucky charm. What does charm mean in this sentence? | A loud song sung at a party | A rude word for a plant | *A tune played on a flute | A small object that people believe brings good luck
exam: Which phrase means to live in comfort? | *Be in clover | Be out of sorts | Be under the weather | Be a bit of a lemon
